One common way the Java API is misused is through the improper handling of user input when interacting with the system shell. This can lead to Command Injection vulnerabilities.

```java
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;

public class CommandExecutor {
    public void pingHost(String hostname) throws Exception {
        // The following line is vulnerable to Command Injection because 
        // it uses a single string containing unsanitized user input.
        // An attacker could pass "google.com; rm -rf /" to execute malicious commands.
        String command = "ping -c 4 " + hostname;

        Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);

        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getInputStream()));
        String line;
        while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
            System.out.println(line);
        }
    }
}
```
